{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head e06df4cf7b9492906f487a22fb6a77f8a567b92f, tree a4753142f7b507a507c5ef293b22505dbfc8f430, on planner/act-env-seventh-20261116, its one artifact 2f00f99a (`notes/2026-11-14-act-environment.md`), for request 498bf861 under my promise 416e0349. This verdict names the one implementation: the seventh amendment (request 0c405d4a, promise cec40ade, report 2f00f99a). `gs review --prepare` resolved that binding at this head. Main 3c8b8b8a is the only parent, and one commit changes only the note.\n\nWhat I checked against the rulings:\n\n- Section 6 matches `77a253b9`, `a6f98773` and the call shape in `3c5b8265`. The view computes `now` for the primary and every `also` and `via`, and it stores nothing. `submit(slot, now)` stops with `shape` before any signature when `now` is missing, ill-shaped or foreign, and also when an editing draft is given one. A scope refusal after a passed exploration costs one more submit, with no hidden retry. On MCP, `act` takes `after` and `now` as a pair.\n- The list arms, the three reasons of a held intention and the optional entry place match `e19f27b5`, `357c2195`, `c79545a3`, `bc447034` and `6d3b979f`. The read-cut rule matches `81711f39`, and the custody fold matches `0967101f`.\n- Section 5.7 matches `695a1839`, `a9056244` (opt-in by `?standing=1`, no new contract export, a largest reply of 5,976 of 16,384 bytes), `25f241cc` and `bb2f7f17` (one export, `judgeExploreGrant`, no type, and one session-ending refusal).\n- Section 10 matches items 1 and 3 of `17e10e32`. Section 7.2 gives the measured cost and the map of `01c542cc`. Section 16 adds the EK-1 row as the owner's exception of 16 November. The status line puts E4 on main `91610da9`.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged, with a 54-character subject. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nAnswers to the five questions:\n\n1. Section 11, row 3 holds now. Under one submit, the draft returns once, either at the exploration or after the scope's refusal, and the next submit signs unless another member acts first. The row says that.\n2. Sections 1 to 18 promise no extra submit, no stored `now` and no two stored forms. One place still says the old rule. The row for `ff578fef` and `481aac4e` in section 19 reads \"A return has two forms. A draft that a refusal returned holds the cause and keeps its basis.\" Section 19 says that \"the sections above hold the results\", so a reader can take that row as current. Mark it as replaced by `77a253b9`.\n3. The sketch misleads. Section 5.1 types `standing` as `readonly FactRef[] | null`, \"the grants at hand\", but section 5.7 now says that the context names the observation, the membership head and the session. Someone who builds E2 from the sketch gets the wrong field. Give the sketch the new shape, or add one comment that ES-1 replaces the field.\n4. The sentence holds. `3c5b8265` gives `primary: ActRef|null`, null \"only for an open act or a comment on null\". The note covers the open act. The comment on null is the one case it leaves out.\n5. Section 10 is right. Section 7.1 does not point to it: \"The instance takes the descriptor digest as a required option\" still reads as the final rule. Add one sentence to 7.1 that the DD-1 proposal replaces the option, as item 4 of `17e10e32` says.\n\nOne more gap against `01c542cc`. Condition 3 asks the note to state the bound of the E4-C map, and the ruling asks where `foldThrough` starts when the replica has a seed. Section 7.2 says that the map holds only the owner's own source entries and that the seed bounds the first fold. It gives no number for the map and does not name the start entry. State both when E4-C lands, or in the next amendment.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The amendment records rulings and adds no new design. One stored shape with a computed `now` removes the second stored form. The standing comes from the session answer and does not need a membership replica.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding. The standing that the session answer carries is only the signer's own, and the reader checks the key, member, membership and incarnation. The value never becomes a grant, and the scope still judges each submit with its own read. `judgeExploreGrant` judges an unsigned body only and never answers `granted`.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The amendment replaces the two-form rule and its extra-submit case with one shape.\n\nThe four points above (the section 19 row, the 5.1 sketch, the 7.1 option and the E4-C bound) do not block this head. The next amendment can fix them.\n\nQualifications that stand: ES-1, EK-1, DD-1 and E4-C are not built, and the note says so. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2f00f99acbe0044d4efaef24ab2ccb7040d76114","binding":"assigned","head":"e06df4cf7b9492906f487a22fb6a77f8a567b92f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:416e03492222d31fbfda6fb5b4f1bbbdedd19d0a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:cec40adef4dfb45df2e9488ca42473a973948cce\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c26920629bf82da372cb69faed64a900a60cfa4f","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}